                        




SCP-5267.



Item #:  SCP-5267

Object Class:  Safe

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5267 is currently stored in a standard locker at Site-26.

Description:  SCP-5267 is a pair of knitted socks. When worn, the wearer occasionally experiences the sensation of a small entity crawling against their foot, described as having multiple haired appendages akin to that of an arachnid. Examination of SCP-5267 during these manifestations reveals no unusual objects.

The sensation ceases if SCP-5267 is removed, or can be interrupted by applying external force to the supposed location of said entity, which results in the feeling of something wet and crunchy bursting within SCP-5267. Due to the original purpose of the object, this is likely to occur while walking or running. No physical changes can be detected.

SCP-5267's anomalous property is noted to manifest at a higher rate during the first stage of non-REM sleep.




Addendum 5267-1:  It was recently determined that SCP-5267's anomalous property can spread to other articles of clothing if placed in close proximity.

Tracking and destroying all possible contaminated items is to be placed on high priority.







                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    

                    
                    
                        
